WEBVTT

1
00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:53.209
Subtitle edited by R3V0LV3R

2
00:01:01.410 --> 00:01:03.291
Do you know what love is?

3
00:01:05.371 --> 00:01:06.891
Real love?

4
00:01:10.611 --> 00:01:13.531
Have you ever loved so deeply...

5
00:01:15.131 --> 00:01:18.132
That you have condemned
yourself to eternity in hell?

6
00:01:20.652 --> 00:01:21.932
I have.

7
00:02:40.537 --> 00:02:41.617
59 seconds.

8
00:02:53.138 --> 00:02:55.058
Dinner for me.

9
00:02:56.618 --> 00:02:59.938
<i>Mr. Picasso,
you haven't signed it.</i>

10
00:03:01.018 --> 00:03:04.019
<i>l said i'm buying dinner,
not the restaurant.</i>

11
00:03:09.219 --> 00:03:10.939
<i>Pablo, have you seen?</i>

12
00:03:11.939 --> 00:03:15.699
<i>Competition, us?
We are all geniuses.</i>

13
00:03:15.859 --> 00:03:21.780
<i>If Picasso doesn't enter,
i, Diego Rivera, i win it again.</i>

14
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.340
-Maybe.
-l thought he was dead.

15
00:03:53.382 --> 00:03:54.662
Jeanne...

16
00:03:55.342 --> 00:03:57.582
What in God's name you think
you are doing?

17
00:03:58.702 --> 00:04:01.382
He needs to see his daughter.

18
00:04:01.582 --> 00:04:04.583
No one should see that
bastard Jew child.

19
00:04:04.743 --> 00:04:07.903
<i>You'll come home now. And,
if you don't obey this moment...</i>

20
00:04:08.023 --> 00:04:12.183
you'll leave me no alternative.

21
00:04:12.743 --> 00:04:15.183
You can't let my baby
live away from me.

22
00:04:15.303 --> 00:04:18.943
You are my daughter.
l can do anything.

23
00:04:22.824 --> 00:04:26.864
I think we should try.

24
00:04:28.824 --> 00:04:30.304
All right.

25
00:04:32.904 --> 00:04:35.425
Stake.
Rare.

26
00:04:50.866 --> 00:04:53.266
<i>Good evening, everyone.</i>

27
00:04:54.306 --> 00:04:56.106
Good evening.

28
00:04:56.266 --> 00:04:59.546
<i>Tonight, l walked
across the bridge.</i>

29
00:04:59.946 --> 00:05:02.786
But there was
no bridge there.

30
00:05:03.706 --> 00:05:06.827
I carried a bag
full of love...

31
00:05:07.307 --> 00:05:10.627
But no one to share it with.

32
00:05:10.787 --> 00:05:12.467
And then...

33
00:05:12.587 --> 00:05:15.427
I thought of you.
All of you.

34
00:05:17.707 --> 00:05:19.747
Love!

35
00:05:24.068 --> 00:05:25.948
We don't have to look
any further.

36
00:05:26.468 --> 00:05:30.108
The future of art
is in a woman's face.

37
00:05:32.268 --> 00:05:34.588
Beautiful.

38
00:05:34.748 --> 00:05:37.069
Pablo Picasso!

39
00:05:37.349 --> 00:05:40.389
<i>Tell me, Pablo,
how do you make love to a cube?</i>

40
00:06:10.591 --> 00:06:12.711
<i>Hello, Pablo.</i>

41
00:06:14.671 --> 00:06:16.551
Did you miss me?

42
00:06:34.872 --> 00:06:36.153
Thank you.

43
00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:41.273
-Good work.
-Why do you hate me so much?

44
00:06:42.513 --> 00:06:44.673
<i>l love you, Pablo.
lt's myself l hate.</i>

45
00:06:51.434 --> 00:06:52.874
Good night.

46
00:06:57.474 --> 00:06:59.074
<i>Music.</i>

47
00:07:00.594 --> 00:07:02.034
What do you think of him?

48
00:07:03.674 --> 00:07:04.874
A God.

49
00:07:17.875 --> 00:07:19.595
How do we do?

50
00:07:22.516 --> 00:07:24.436
Sooner or later somebody
will catch on.

51
00:07:25.756 --> 00:07:28.596
<i>Get out of that, Modigliani.
You need sun.</i>

52
00:07:28.716 --> 00:07:29.956
And let you starve?

53
00:07:30.036 --> 00:07:32.076
I don't think l could have
that on my conscience.

54
00:07:32.156 --> 00:07:33.996
Good night.

55
00:07:35.316 --> 00:07:38.677
<i>-Modi, what do l do?
-Save it for Beatrice.</i>

56
00:07:58.598 --> 00:08:02.358
-You can't change destiny.
-What destiny?

57
00:08:02.718 --> 00:08:06.398
Hers.
To be with him.

58
00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:34.000
Stay here.

59
00:08:37.521 --> 00:08:39.441
Come here.

60
00:08:48.081 --> 00:08:50.321
This dog is stupid.

61
00:08:50.921 --> 00:08:52.482
<i>Wait, wait.</i>

62
00:08:53.762 --> 00:08:55.762
Here.

63
00:08:56.282 --> 00:08:58.162
Come here.

64
00:08:58.362 --> 00:09:00.482
Here it is.

65
00:09:00.642 --> 00:09:02.482
lt's all right.

66
00:09:02.642 --> 00:09:04.122
Come here.

67
00:09:06.242 --> 00:09:08.683
Come here.

68
00:10:09.847 --> 00:10:11.407
Jeanne...

69
00:10:12.567 --> 00:10:14.287
How do you know my name?

70
00:10:15.807 --> 00:10:18.407
I had to.
l am...

71
00:10:18.527 --> 00:10:22.127
Modigliani. l know who you are.
We all know who you are.

72
00:10:22.407 --> 00:10:24.928
Even the dog knew
who you were.

73
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:27.208
<i>Come, l wanna see you
in the rain.</i>

74
00:10:28.768 --> 00:10:30.448
Don't be afraid.

75
00:10:31.848 --> 00:10:35.648
I love the rain.
l love what it says.

76
00:10:35.808 --> 00:10:38.969
How interesting.
Now the rain speaks.

77
00:10:39.129 --> 00:10:41.289
-Yes.
-What does it say?

78
00:10:41.529 --> 00:10:43.649
Says you need a hat.

79
00:10:44.289 --> 00:10:46.809
Thank you.

80
00:10:48.089 --> 00:10:50.489
First you have to show me
your drawing.

81
00:10:50.689 --> 00:10:55.890
-I'm not an artist.
-You let me tell you that.

82
00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:59.010
<i>No drawing,
no hat.</i>

83
00:11:01.330 --> 00:11:04.890
-Okay. The hat first.
-Hat first.

84
00:11:30.332 --> 00:11:31.772
This is how you see me?

85
00:11:32.292 --> 00:11:34.812
That's how everybody
see Modigliani.

86
00:11:40.453 --> 00:11:41.933
I'm sorry.

87
00:11:46.213 --> 00:11:48.293
Call me Modi.

88
00:11:50.213 --> 00:11:51.733
<i>Okay, Modi.</i>

89
00:11:55.014 --> 00:11:58.214
Now i'll paint you. You come
see me and i'll paint you.

90
00:11:59.134 --> 00:12:01.574
-If i'm lucky one day...
-What?

91
00:12:04.134 --> 00:12:06.614
I'll paint your eyes.

92
00:12:07.814 --> 00:12:11.855
With your reputation?
You think i'm crazy?

93
00:12:36.696 --> 00:12:38.176
What do you think?

94
00:12:40.497 --> 00:12:42.497
Where are my eyes?

95
00:12:52.537 --> 00:12:54.978
<i>Too far away,
l couldn't see them.</i>

96
00:13:13.979 --> 00:13:16.259
<i>When l know your soul,
i'll paint your eyes.</i>

97
00:13:41.541 --> 00:13:43.781
Look at daddy's work.

98
00:13:45.621 --> 00:13:48.501
<i>You're very late, monsieur.
Everybody's waiting for you.</i>

99
00:13:50.421 --> 00:13:51.581
Excuse me.

100
00:13:52.301 --> 00:13:54.702
Beautiful.

101
00:13:55.222 --> 00:13:58.662
You have beautiful bones.
l could paint you.

102
00:13:58.822 --> 00:14:00.942
Ten Francs.
Talk to Martinez.

103
00:14:01.182 --> 00:14:03.142
<i>The one and only, Martinez.</i>

104
00:14:09.062 --> 00:14:12.183
You keep them waiting.
it's not fair.

105
00:14:12.303 --> 00:14:15.663
They've got a lot of money
and no taste.

106
00:14:16.903 --> 00:14:18.263
I'm a buyer.

107
00:14:18.383 --> 00:14:20.783
<i>Even though you've kept me waiting,
l think your paintings are...</i>

108
00:14:21.503 --> 00:14:23.143
interesting.

109
00:14:24.023 --> 00:14:27.424
Interesting?

110
00:14:28.944 --> 00:14:31.904
<i>He's got galleries
in New York, Modi.</i>

111
00:14:34.584 --> 00:14:36.184
Really?

112
00:14:38.944 --> 00:14:41.625
Biggest galleries in New York?
Interesting.

113
00:14:41.745 --> 00:14:42.945
That's funny.

114
00:14:43.025 --> 00:14:46.345
<i>Like you said, they've got money
but no taste.</i>

115
00:14:48.225 --> 00:14:49.705
Very funny.

116
00:15:00.786 --> 00:15:04.706
<i>Modigliani,
how dare you embarrass me?</i>

117
00:15:05.666 --> 00:15:07.546
Where are you going?

118
00:15:18.107 --> 00:15:19.227
Go back to your sheep.

119
00:15:19.707 --> 00:15:22.827
<i>If you walk away,
don't come back.</i>

120
00:15:23.307 --> 00:15:25.068
<i>Farewell, Martinez.</i>

121
00:16:35.992 --> 00:16:37.232
Search the house.

122
00:16:41.233 --> 00:16:44.593
Lt is here stated
that the Modigliani family...

123
00:16:44.753 --> 00:16:49.193
<i>in fare taxes, owes to
the Italian Republic.</i>

124
00:16:49.393 --> 00:16:52.913
it's therefore stated that
the Modigliani family...

125
00:16:53.033 --> 00:16:56.034
<i>shall be relieved of all properties,
household or other items...</i>

126
00:16:56.154 --> 00:17:00.234
that can be sold for the purpose
of the Italian Republic.

127
00:17:00.794 --> 00:17:03.154
Ancient law of Italy states...

128
00:17:03.274 --> 00:17:08.834
<i>whatever a pregnant woman has
in the bed, she can keep.</i>

129
00:17:09.834 --> 00:17:11.795
We claim this right.

130
00:17:11.955 --> 00:17:16.395
-Jews were never fool.
-Son of a bitch.

131
00:17:16.475 --> 00:17:20.995
Are you not going to write down
everything we have on the bed?

132
00:17:21.115 --> 00:17:23.435
Don't worry.
l intend to do so.

133
00:17:23.595 --> 00:17:24.955
Five chairs...

134
00:17:25.755 --> 00:17:28.036
Two chandeliers...

135
00:17:29.116 --> 00:17:31.356
Two tables...

136
00:17:32.476 --> 00:17:34.396
Three blankets

137
00:17:36.156 --> 00:17:38.476
four paintings...

138
00:17:39.196 --> 00:17:41.877
One large mirror...

139
00:17:44.157 --> 00:17:46.037
One base...

140
00:17:47.637 --> 00:17:50.757
Two carpets...

141
00:17:50.997 --> 00:17:53.837
Two holds...

142
00:17:56.278 --> 00:17:58.078
A sewing machine...

143
00:18:05.438 --> 00:18:07.598
Mama...

144
00:18:08.478 --> 00:18:10.038
Papa...

145
00:18:13.879 --> 00:18:14.999
Grandpa...

146
00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:39.560
Amen.

147
00:18:57.162 --> 00:19:00.722
<i>Help me, father.
What have l done wrong?</i>

148
00:19:01.602 --> 00:19:05.122
l fell in love.
ls that a sin?

149
00:19:05.762 --> 00:19:07.682
<i>No, my dear.</i>

150
00:19:08.282 --> 00:19:11.442
The sin would be
to never have loved at all.

151
00:19:12.003 --> 00:19:13.723
I don't know what to do.

152
00:19:15.323 --> 00:19:18.123
I don't know what l want.

153
00:19:19.523 --> 00:19:21.123
I miss him.

154
00:19:22.243 --> 00:19:24.283
I miss him.

155
00:19:24.483 --> 00:19:26.043
I can't lose him.

156
00:19:27.524 --> 00:19:29.684
Why does one man
hate another...

157
00:19:30.124 --> 00:19:32.724
Just because of his faith?

158
00:19:32.884 --> 00:19:35.364
<i>The church doesn't hate Modi,
does it, Father?</i>

159
00:19:36.004 --> 00:19:38.324
The church is not
the enemy here.

160
00:19:39.844 --> 00:19:42.485
Your faith is not the enemy.

161
00:19:42.605 --> 00:19:46.525
You must be strong
for you and for the baby.

162
00:19:54.565 --> 00:19:58.926
<i>lt is for the best.
You'll see, my dear.</i>

163
00:19:59.046 --> 00:20:03.206
The world is a cruel place
for a child who has a stigma.

164
00:20:18.527 --> 00:20:21.807
<i>Stop.
Stop, look at me.</i>

165
00:20:23.247 --> 00:20:25.887
You stupid girl.

166
00:20:26.047 --> 00:20:28.848
You are a child. You do not know
what you are doing.

167
00:20:28.968 --> 00:20:32.448
<i>And do you? Do you know
what you're doing, papa?</i>

168
00:20:33.328 --> 00:20:36.008
Remember what you did?
Remember?

169
00:21:08.730 --> 00:21:12.050
Poor bastards. They don't even
know what they'll fight for.

170
00:21:12.170 --> 00:21:14.931
They're not supposed to.

171
00:21:22.731 --> 00:21:24.691
Stop the car.

172
00:21:27.691 --> 00:21:29.332
Modigliani!

173
00:21:34.892 --> 00:21:39.172
You do not walk out on me.
l walk out on you.

174
00:21:39.452 --> 00:21:42.332
For the damage.
Buy everyone a drink.

175
00:21:42.612 --> 00:21:45.133
But not for you.
l stopped that.

176
00:21:48.613 --> 00:21:49.773
Drive on.

177
00:22:22.095 --> 00:22:25.655
-l think she's over there.
-it's a she?

178
00:22:30.016 --> 00:22:34.896
<i>Excuse me, monsieur. Are you
looking for Maurice Utrillo?</i>

179
00:22:35.216 --> 00:22:36.936
Who are you?

180
00:22:37.016 --> 00:22:38.896
I'm a strangled chicken.

181
00:22:39.016 --> 00:22:41.976
Why don't you help me?
l do.

182
00:22:42.216 --> 00:22:43.777
I found her!

183
00:22:45.617 --> 00:22:48.377
Isn't she glorious?

184
00:22:49.617 --> 00:22:52.297
She's gonna win
the competition.

185
00:22:52.377 --> 00:22:55.217
-You never said anything about it.
-You never asked.

186
00:22:55.337 --> 00:22:57.417
<i>-Come on, help me.
-This is meat.</i>

187
00:22:58.417 --> 00:23:00.658
Get this of my face.

188
00:23:03.338 --> 00:23:05.298
Shit.

189
00:23:08.778 --> 00:23:09.858
<i>Good evening, ladies.</i>

190
00:23:45.301 --> 00:23:47.621
-l love you.
-l love you.

191
00:23:47.701 --> 00:23:49.181
I love you.

192
00:23:52.661 --> 00:23:55.981
-l missed you.
-Let's take care of that.

193
00:23:58.781 --> 00:24:00.182
Where have you been?

194
00:24:01.262 --> 00:24:03.142
Looking for you.

195
00:24:22.903 --> 00:24:25.383
-Like that?
-That's beautiful.

196
00:26:00.790 --> 00:26:02.110
Where are you going?

197
00:26:04.990 --> 00:26:06.910
Where are you going?

198
00:26:07.350 --> 00:26:08.950
What's wrong?

199
00:26:13.630 --> 00:26:16.791
Have you looked around?

200
00:26:18.991 --> 00:26:22.311
You think it's right a baby
come to a place like this?

201
00:26:25.271 --> 00:26:29.511
Look at me.
l have nothing for you.

202
00:26:30.271 --> 00:26:31.992
I am nothing.

203
00:26:32.992 --> 00:26:35.912
I am nothing.

204
00:26:39.832 --> 00:26:42.592
I can't be a father
to my own child.

205
00:26:44.432 --> 00:26:46.033
I can't.

206
00:26:48.593 --> 00:26:52.793
<i>So, that's it.
You just run away.</i>

207
00:26:52.953 --> 00:26:54.833
l do best.

208
00:27:02.914 --> 00:27:05.594
<i>-I'm sorry.
-No, you're not.</i>

209
00:27:05.674 --> 00:27:08.074
You're too damn selfish
to be sorry.

210
00:27:08.234 --> 00:27:10.634
I walked away from my baby
to be with you.

211
00:27:10.754 --> 00:27:12.274
You should go back.

212
00:27:12.434 --> 00:27:14.714
You can be the girl you were
when l first met you.

213
00:27:14.874 --> 00:27:16.875
Remember her?
Remember?

214
00:27:17.155 --> 00:27:20.275
Would she put up with this?

215
00:27:22.715 --> 00:27:24.955
No.

216
00:27:25.075 --> 00:27:26.515
Would she put up with me?

217
00:27:27.155 --> 00:27:28.555
No.

218
00:27:36.196 --> 00:27:37.356
This one?

219
00:27:37.716 --> 00:27:38.956
Why not?

220
00:27:39.076 --> 00:27:42.276
<i>l don't know which painting
you want. Point, or choose.</i>

221
00:27:43.676 --> 00:27:50.637
The Matisse.
What big guy we have to take.

222
00:27:57.757 --> 00:27:59.757
Very well.

223
00:27:59.877 --> 00:28:02.918
<i>Jeanne, how are you?
How is Modi?</i>

224
00:28:03.078 --> 00:28:05.718
l haven't seen him.
l didn't know where he is.

225
00:28:11.118 --> 00:28:13.478
-What is the problem?
-l need your help.

226
00:28:13.598 --> 00:28:14.998
What is it?

227
00:28:15.158 --> 00:28:17.279
I want you to go to Picasso.

228
00:28:17.479 --> 00:28:21.319
Ask him to hang his artwork
beside his in the new exhibition.

229
00:28:24.279 --> 00:28:26.879
<i>Yes, anything.</i>

230
00:28:27.159 --> 00:28:29.159
Zbo!

231
00:28:29.639 --> 00:28:32.440
Modi and Picasso...

232
00:28:33.200 --> 00:28:35.760
Modi will kill me
if l do such a thing.

233
00:28:36.680 --> 00:28:40.240
<i>I'm sorry, Jeanne.
l can't.</i>

234
00:28:40.360 --> 00:28:44.280
<i>If Modi's work hang beside Pablo's,
there's a chance of good sale.</i>

235
00:28:45.320 --> 00:28:48.401
<i>We need money, Zbo.
Please.</i>

236
00:28:48.801 --> 00:28:50.121
Please!

237
00:28:50.601 --> 00:28:52.561
I love you both.

238
00:28:52.681 --> 00:28:54.561
But you're better off
with your family.

239
00:28:54.681 --> 00:28:58.641
At least the child would have
a better chance in life.

240
00:29:02.282 --> 00:29:04.122
I am wasting my breath.

241
00:29:04.362 --> 00:29:07.122
I'm always wasting
my breath.

242
00:29:07.322 --> 00:29:09.402
Let's think.

243
00:29:19.603 --> 00:29:21.163
I know.

244
00:29:23.363 --> 00:29:27.883
lt's something you could do.

245
00:29:29.283 --> 00:29:31.523
lt will be bold.

246
00:29:31.683 --> 00:29:34.524
lt's his way to say he's sorry
for the other night.

247
00:29:34.684 --> 00:29:37.684
For the other night?
And the nights before that?

248
00:29:38.604 --> 00:29:42.564
<i>Let me see, one canvas
per insult.</i>

249
00:29:42.684 --> 00:29:46.164
<i>-Olga, how many?
-Hundreds, Pablo.</i>

250
00:29:53.365 --> 00:29:57.285
<i>Let me paint you, Jeanne.
I'll make you immortal.</i>

251
00:29:57.405 --> 00:30:00.925
That's just too much responsibility
for these shoulders.

252
00:30:09.206 --> 00:30:10.966
My answer is no.

253
00:30:17.967 --> 00:30:19.447
Wait.

254
00:30:29.607 --> 00:30:33.728
Look handsome
like Modigliani?

255
00:30:34.608 --> 00:30:37.048
There's just no comparison.

256
00:30:39.088 --> 00:30:42.888
<i>He'll hang one painting,
but there is one condition.</i>

257
00:30:57.969 --> 00:30:59.489
You can go now.

258
00:31:04.210 --> 00:31:10.410
-You're up to something. What?
-Keep dusting.

259
00:31:13.250 --> 00:31:14.650
Modi!

260
00:31:15.250 --> 00:31:17.130
Modigliani!

261
00:31:17.250 --> 00:31:18.531
Where is he?

262
00:31:20.531 --> 00:31:23.011
Finally.

263
00:31:23.531 --> 00:31:26.251
<i>-Oh, shit.
-What you want with my son, bastard?</i>

264
00:31:27.131 --> 00:31:28.211
Good.

265
00:31:28.451 --> 00:31:29.491
Wait.

266
00:31:30.211 --> 00:31:32.011
Hold that.

267
00:31:32.131 --> 00:31:34.612
You haven't sold a painting
in 6 months. Kill him.

268
00:31:36.532 --> 00:31:40.652
<i>You shoot me, you can kiss yourself
goodbye. l won't organize it.</i>

269
00:31:44.692 --> 00:31:46.652
-Stop.
-You said l could kill him.

270
00:31:46.772 --> 00:31:48.493
Later.
Kill him later.

271
00:31:50.693 --> 00:31:54.053
<i>Come out, you coward.
Come have some wine.</i>

272
00:32:09.494 --> 00:32:12.334
<i>Please, take this.</i>

273
00:32:13.814 --> 00:32:16.174
<i>Modi, have you given thought
of the competition?</i>

274
00:32:16.254 --> 00:32:18.175
The prize gives a lot of money.

275
00:32:21.855 --> 00:32:24.815
The whole Paris is dreaming
of the day.

276
00:32:24.895 --> 00:32:26.695
You and Picasso
compete together.

277
00:32:26.855 --> 00:32:28.775
<i>Yes, me and Picasso.</i>

278
00:32:30.415 --> 00:32:32.735
You said something
about a show?

279
00:32:32.895 --> 00:32:36.176
lt's not much of a show.
lt's more of a favor.

280
00:32:36.256 --> 00:32:39.456
Pablo has offered to hang one of
your paintings in his exhibition.

281
00:32:40.496 --> 00:32:42.536
A favor?

282
00:32:42.936 --> 00:32:46.456
Pablo Picasso is doing
Modigliani a favor?

283
00:32:46.576 --> 00:32:50.257
-What's the matter with you?
-You have to care now.

284
00:32:50.737 --> 00:32:53.137
lt is your family
with Jeanne.

285
00:32:53.257 --> 00:32:55.577
You wanna do me a favor?

286
00:32:56.617 --> 00:32:59.177
<i>-l need money for a doctor.
-No, Modi, please.</i>

287
00:32:59.257 --> 00:33:01.617
l need money
for a doctor.

288
00:33:01.737 --> 00:33:03.858
Promise me you'll not
drink it all away.

289
00:33:04.538 --> 00:33:06.898
<i>Okay, take your picture.</i>

290
00:33:13.378 --> 00:33:15.258
What if the doctor drinks?

291
00:33:24.339 --> 00:33:26.459
Am l dying?

292
00:33:27.419 --> 00:33:29.899
You said you had tuberculosis
as a child.

293
00:33:30.819 --> 00:33:33.379
But l feel much better now.

294
00:33:34.740 --> 00:33:36.980
lt never left you.

295
00:33:38.140 --> 00:33:39.740
You can dress now.

296
00:33:40.700 --> 00:33:44.020
Your lungs are working with
less than half their capacity.

297
00:33:44.980 --> 00:33:48.540
If you continue to use
drugs and alcohol...

298
00:33:48.780 --> 00:33:51.061
You will not live
past this year.

299
00:33:52.061 --> 00:33:53.941
This medicine will help
your cough.

300
00:35:09.866 --> 00:35:12.546
-Maybe you shouldn't go there.
-Fuck them.

301
00:35:14.306 --> 00:35:15.946
Put on some horns.
Come on.

302
00:35:22.587 --> 00:35:25.787
-Why are you so nervous?
-Nothing.

303
00:35:26.507 --> 00:35:30.307
-What did the doctor say?
-She said l should find a new agent.

304
00:35:30.427 --> 00:35:31.707
Good.

305
00:35:31.867 --> 00:35:34.868
Let's get out of here.
I'm fed up with them.

306
00:35:36.748 --> 00:35:41.068
<i>-There he is.
-Good evening, gentlemen.</i>

307
00:35:41.348 --> 00:35:44.588
<i>Modi, what do you have
to say for yourself?</i>

308
00:35:44.708 --> 00:35:47.628
<i>-Hello, Gertrude.
-Don't Gertrude me.</i>

309
00:35:48.268 --> 00:35:51.709
Four days i've waited.
For days!

310
00:35:52.349 --> 00:35:54.749
Am l not good enough to paint?
Not pretty enough perhaps?

311
00:35:55.229 --> 00:35:59.669
These eyes are not so good to paint
something so sophisticated.

312
00:36:00.509 --> 00:36:04.229
Bold.
Horse shit!

313
00:36:04.709 --> 00:36:07.590
<i>Tomorrow morning, my apartment,
ten o'clock sharp.</i>

314
00:36:07.710 --> 00:36:09.270
<i>Sharp, you hear me?</i>

315
00:36:09.390 --> 00:36:12.230
Do not worry. l promise you.
He will be there.

316
00:36:12.430 --> 00:36:14.550
Ladies and gentlemen...

317
00:36:14.710 --> 00:36:17.470
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, may l have
your attention please?</i>

318
00:36:17.630 --> 00:36:23.911
Welcome to the 10th exhibition
of work of the artist Picasso.

319
00:36:24.071 --> 00:36:26.271
<i>And Modigliani, asshole!</i>

320
00:36:26.431 --> 00:36:29.351
And the distinct works
of Modigliani.

321
00:36:36.832 --> 00:36:41.712
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
l give you Picasso...</i>

322
00:36:42.192 --> 00:36:45.232
to work your progress.

323
00:36:50.312 --> 00:36:53.033
<i>Oh, no.</i>

324
00:38:25.039 --> 00:38:26.559
<i>Modi, wait.</i>

325
00:38:26.879 --> 00:38:28.359
Wait!

326
00:38:31.119 --> 00:38:33.639
I did it for you.
To help you.

327
00:38:33.839 --> 00:38:38.240
-l don't need that kind of help.
-Fine. Do it for your baby.

328
00:38:39.400 --> 00:38:44.120
You know what she needs?
She needs you.

329
00:38:44.560 --> 00:38:46.360
<i>Yes, she needs you.</i>

330
00:38:53.041 --> 00:38:55.601
<i>Yes, it's papa.</i>

331
00:38:55.761 --> 00:38:57.921
-He should go.
-Why?

332
00:38:58.001 --> 00:39:00.961
Your father will be home soon.
He can't be here.

333
00:39:01.041 --> 00:39:02.761
Can l come with him?

334
00:39:02.921 --> 00:39:08.642
Then what? Let him
abuse you again? Destroy you?

335
00:39:08.762 --> 00:39:12.402
I don't wanna hear.
l don't wanna hear that.

336
00:39:16.082 --> 00:39:17.482
<i>Modi, let's go.</i>

337
00:39:26.723 --> 00:39:28.163
l told him.

338
00:39:28.283 --> 00:39:32.843
I warned you. if you choose
to be with that Jew...

339
00:39:33.683 --> 00:39:37.884
I would have no alternative but
to inform the authorities...

340
00:39:38.004 --> 00:39:40.164
That you are an unfit mother.

341
00:39:40.244 --> 00:39:45.924
<i>After which, they'll take your child
and you'll never see her again.</i>

342
00:39:58.365 --> 00:39:59.845
See how beautiful she is?

343
00:40:02.285 --> 00:40:04.645
Look at her.
Look at her.

344
00:40:29.207 --> 00:40:30.527
Granpapa...

345
00:40:45.568 --> 00:40:47.328
I'll be watching you.

346
00:41:43.092 --> 00:41:45.172
<i>Hello, Madame Stein.</i>

347
00:41:45.852 --> 00:41:47.172
So?

348
00:41:47.652 --> 00:41:49.012
What?

349
00:41:49.172 --> 00:41:51.092
<i>Jeanne, you dummy.</i>

350
00:41:51.252 --> 00:41:54.013
That was a clever stroke
she played there last night.

351
00:41:54.453 --> 00:41:56.133
<i>Right girl, that one.</i>

352
00:41:56.493 --> 00:41:59.173
<i>So, did you kiss
and make out?</i>

353
00:42:05.053 --> 00:42:06.613
She's better off without me.

354
00:42:08.534 --> 00:42:10.774
My abandoned ass!

355
00:42:15.854 --> 00:42:19.254
-Do you want some advice?
-Do l have a choice?

356
00:42:19.454 --> 00:42:22.734
<i>Oh, no.
Enter the competition.</i>

357
00:42:23.615 --> 00:42:26.575
<i>l bet the minute you do,
Pablo will too.</i>

358
00:42:27.975 --> 00:42:32.415
Never.
He's too proud.

359
00:42:33.335 --> 00:42:35.095
<i>Plus, he doesn't need the money.</i>

360
00:42:38.256 --> 00:42:40.776
Maybe.
But you do.

361
00:42:44.776 --> 00:42:45.976
You're right.

362
00:42:54.057 --> 00:42:56.377
-With or without?
-What?

363
00:42:56.577 --> 00:42:58.617
The cream on your mouth.

364
00:43:01.457 --> 00:43:02.777
Let's go.

365
00:43:08.337 --> 00:43:10.138
<i>Give me one good reason why.</i>

366
00:43:10.258 --> 00:43:13.978
<i>Rivera, Kisling, Utrillo,
Soutine...</i>

367
00:43:16.538 --> 00:43:19.938
Modigliani.
You just said the wrong name.

368
00:43:20.098 --> 00:43:23.458
<i>Olga, tell him he must compete
in the competition.</i>

369
00:43:24.099 --> 00:43:26.859
You must compete
in the competition.

370
00:43:29.299 --> 00:43:30.939
I'm making dinner.
How was?

371
00:43:31.059 --> 00:43:32.419
Straight.

372
00:43:33.459 --> 00:43:36.819
Who told you he'll be there?

373
00:43:36.979 --> 00:43:39.740
Gertrude.
He has a scratch.

374
00:43:39.940 --> 00:43:42.660
He needs the money badly.
He has no choice.

375
00:43:43.140 --> 00:43:46.140
I don't believe her.
She lies for a living.

376
00:43:46.340 --> 00:43:48.740
<i>Please, Pablo.</i>

377
00:43:49.860 --> 00:43:51.260
it will be so much fun.

378
00:43:51.620 --> 00:43:54.301
Paris has become so tedious
since the war.

379
00:43:54.501 --> 00:43:56.381
Let's bring back the life.

380
00:43:56.541 --> 00:43:59.781
<i>Fine works, champagne.
All night drinking and laughing.</i>

381
00:44:00.741 --> 00:44:03.661
Get into the ring.
Play with the bull.

382
00:44:06.661 --> 00:44:08.781
I am the bull.

383
00:44:13.102 --> 00:44:16.382
Fish.
Let's eat.

384
00:44:20.902 --> 00:44:22.422
I love it.

385
00:44:55.345 --> 00:44:57.025
<i>Modigliani!</i>

386
00:44:57.145 --> 00:44:58.785
<i>Pablo!</i>

387
00:44:58.945 --> 00:45:01.985
<i>How are you,
Amedeo Modigliani?</i>

388
00:45:02.145 --> 00:45:04.105
What do you call it?

389
00:45:05.705 --> 00:45:07.705
lt's a great day.

390
00:45:09.546 --> 00:45:12.026
<i>Good morning, matador.</i>

391
00:45:13.466 --> 00:45:18.946
Let me ask you a question.
You have entered the competition?

392
00:45:21.426 --> 00:45:23.186
Answer me!

393
00:46:18.110 --> 00:46:19.670
<i>Don't touch my work!</i>

394
00:46:19.870 --> 00:46:22.670
<i>Don't touch my work!
You don't have the right.</i>

395
00:46:22.830 --> 00:46:25.951
<i>Get your hands off of my work!</i>

396
00:46:40.792 --> 00:46:45.232
You have money?

397
00:46:48.152 --> 00:46:52.512
I can make you very happy
if you have money.

398
00:46:53.552 --> 00:46:55.313
I have nothing.

399
00:46:57.553 --> 00:46:59.433
<i>Run!</i>

400
00:47:03.553 --> 00:47:06.273
Police!

401
00:47:25.875 --> 00:47:28.795
<i>Are you okay, Modi?</i>

402
00:47:30.515 --> 00:47:32.395
Who paid the fine?

403
00:47:33.115 --> 00:47:34.515
Who paid the fine?

404
00:47:34.675 --> 00:47:37.115
We don't know. Whoever it was
didn't want to say.

405
00:47:37.235 --> 00:47:38.555
Find out.

406
00:47:38.675 --> 00:47:41.476
<i>If i find out who it was, i'd first
try to sell him your paintings.</i>

407
00:47:41.716 --> 00:47:43.676
Then l will thank you.

408
00:47:47.116 --> 00:47:50.436
What?

409
00:47:51.596 --> 00:47:54.156
lt's Utrillo.

410
00:47:55.356 --> 00:47:58.757
-What?
-He's back in the asylum.

411
00:47:58.997 --> 00:48:01.757
His mother told the police
and they put him away.

412
00:48:01.997 --> 00:48:05.237
<i>Modi, this is a sign from God
that things must change.</i>

413
00:48:05.397 --> 00:48:07.837
Where was God when Utrillo
needed Him?

414
00:48:19.638 --> 00:48:23.118
You've got here too late.
Should have seen this morning.

415
00:48:23.998 --> 00:48:26.519
Your father visited the child's
welfare this morning.

416
00:48:27.959 --> 00:48:30.839
He's recommended they take
custody of the baby.

417
00:48:34.559 --> 00:48:36.159
Did you hear me?

418
00:48:37.999 --> 00:48:40.079
-You're going to lose your child.
-l have no choice!

419
00:48:40.279 --> 00:48:43.760
-Your child.
-l have no choice!

420
00:48:43.960 --> 00:48:48.160
You could choose your baby.

421
00:48:49.200 --> 00:48:51.400
He's dying.

422
00:48:53.080 --> 00:48:55.280
You're dying with him.

423
00:49:46.644 --> 00:49:50.564
<i>Maurice, it's me, Modi.</i>

424
00:49:52.204 --> 00:49:54.724
it's me.

425
00:50:10.485 --> 00:50:12.686
lt's okay.

426
00:50:24.646 --> 00:50:27.607
Everything will be fine.
i'll get you out of here.

427
00:50:29.207 --> 00:50:33.847
lt's an old dream.
You know this is my life.

428
00:50:34.047 --> 00:50:36.727
She won't be sorry for me.
She'll be happy.

429
00:50:36.887 --> 00:50:39.927
You mad bastard.

430
00:50:46.008 --> 00:50:47.888
A little haxixe?

431
00:51:10.169 --> 00:51:14.170
-Promise me.
-Promise you what?

432
00:51:14.610 --> 00:51:16.690
That you won't let me die here.

433
00:51:17.730 --> 00:51:21.050
I've seen what they do
with buddies around here.

434
00:51:22.650 --> 00:51:25.970
I don't want that.
Promise me.

435
00:51:26.890 --> 00:51:28.731
I don't know.

436
00:51:30.251 --> 00:51:34.211
I promise.

437
00:51:35.971 --> 00:51:38.331
-I'm cold.
-It's okay. i got you.

438
00:51:38.491 --> 00:51:40.371
I wish l could hug you.

439
00:51:40.931 --> 00:51:42.652
I'm so cold.

440
00:52:23.654 --> 00:52:27.854
Welcome.
I'm overwhelmed.

441
00:52:28.815 --> 00:52:33.415
<i>-Jeanne, you look great.
-You look gorgeous.</i>

442
00:52:34.815 --> 00:52:37.815
l love your shoes.

443
00:52:38.175 --> 00:52:40.215
-Enjoy the party.
-Thank you.

444
00:52:42.375 --> 00:52:45.056
-You should thank Picasso.
-For what?

445
00:52:45.256 --> 00:52:48.216
For letting you out.

446
00:52:53.096 --> 00:52:54.776
Modi!

447
00:52:55.976 --> 00:52:58.337
What a nice vision!

448
00:52:59.337 --> 00:53:00.817
Dance?

449
00:53:02.377 --> 00:53:05.337
-Modi.
-Thank you.

450
00:53:05.537 --> 00:53:07.137
Pablo is over there.

451
00:53:17.898 --> 00:53:20.938
-The famous Picasso.
-Matador.

452
00:53:27.618 --> 00:53:29.619
I didn't ask you to bail me out.

453
00:53:29.739 --> 00:53:32.219
You want to pay me back?
Let's see.

454
00:53:34.219 --> 00:53:39.019
Why don't you come tomorrow? We'll
go to a trip to the countryside.

455
00:53:39.419 --> 00:53:41.539
There's somebody
l want you to meet.

456
00:53:41.659 --> 00:53:45.420
-Only if Olga comes.
-You really like my wife?

457
00:53:46.700 --> 00:53:49.860
Everybody really likes your wife.

458
00:53:57.100 --> 00:53:59.701
Tonight is a night
for dancing.

459
00:53:59.821 --> 00:54:01.901
When a samurai
gets his sword...

460
00:54:02.141 --> 00:54:04.261
He must draw blood.

461
00:55:18.906 --> 00:55:19.946
Who lives here?

462
00:55:21.746 --> 00:55:24.306
You'll see.

463
00:55:56.068 --> 00:56:00.069
-Renoir.
-Come meet God.

464
00:56:35.911 --> 00:56:37.951
This man looks mad.

465
00:56:42.031 --> 00:56:44.151
Are you mad?

466
00:56:50.232 --> 00:56:54.592
They scare you.
Deformity.

467
00:56:54.952 --> 00:56:58.672
The genius sucked out
through the fingernails.

468
00:57:00.673 --> 00:57:02.273
They don't bother me.

469
00:57:03.193 --> 00:57:08.153
<i>Liar.
He's a liar, Pablo?</i>

470
00:57:11.953 --> 00:57:15.754
<i>May l ask you, how much
a place like this cost?</i>

471
00:57:15.954 --> 00:57:18.834
Two paintings.
Small.

472
00:57:19.474 --> 00:57:24.314
I have two cars in the stables.
A scratch for each.

473
00:57:24.634 --> 00:57:28.154
And this Rodin.

474
00:57:28.354 --> 00:57:33.155
I gave one little pencil drawing
of a flowerpot.

475
00:57:33.595 --> 00:57:37.435
No flower.
Just a pot.

476
00:57:40.315 --> 00:57:42.075
You into sell?

477
00:57:44.515 --> 00:57:46.756
Modigliani is on the verge.

478
00:57:48.276 --> 00:57:51.636
On the verge.
Let's say no.

479
00:57:51.876 --> 00:57:53.716
"Le précipice."
The cliff.

480
00:57:54.356 --> 00:58:01.357
Where all artists converge
and jump to their fate.

481
00:58:08.717 --> 00:58:16.198
<i>Nudes mostly, occasional
portraits, drink...</i>

482
00:58:16.878 --> 00:58:19.158
-Yes?
-Yes.

483
00:58:20.118 --> 00:58:24.758
-How did you know?
-Pablo told me.

484
00:58:27.558 --> 00:58:30.798
I've never liked
painting nudes myself.

485
00:58:31.599 --> 00:58:35.159
Most of the women in my time
were too fat.

486
00:58:35.799 --> 00:58:39.919
And ugly.
Very ugly.

487
00:58:40.879 --> 00:58:45.559
I like them tall and slim.

488
00:58:46.120 --> 00:58:50.000
<i>So, it's late.
We should go.</i>

489
00:59:00.840 --> 00:59:04.121
Amedeo Modigliani...

490
00:59:06.201 --> 00:59:08.881
Are you mad?

491
00:59:21.602 --> 00:59:23.682
I knew that.

492
00:59:32.163 --> 00:59:33.963
You'll enter the competition?

493
00:59:36.203 --> 00:59:37.523
Will you?

494
00:59:39.643 --> 00:59:41.763
You see what painting
can bring?

495
00:59:42.683 --> 00:59:45.523
<i>Comfort, wealth, security.</i>

496
00:59:46.083 --> 00:59:50.124
Only a fool starts to starve.
Paris is trying them.

497
00:59:51.124 --> 00:59:56.404
<i>So paint, make money, get old,
fuck as many women as you can...</i>

498
00:59:56.644 --> 01:00:00.004
but drink with moderation.

499
01:00:02.965 --> 01:00:05.685
The gospel according to Picasso.

500
01:00:13.125 --> 01:00:16.525
You can't fight me now.

501
01:00:17.366 --> 01:00:21.206
<i>So let me ask you,
are you mocking me?</i>

502
01:00:25.206 --> 01:00:26.526
l try.

503
01:00:27.806 --> 01:00:30.486
Sometimes l don't succeed.
Sometimes...

504
01:00:31.206 --> 01:00:35.807
<i>You see, Modi, there is a difference
between you and me...</i>

505
01:00:37.407 --> 01:00:39.207
success.

506
01:00:39.367 --> 01:00:41.407
lt is.

507
01:00:56.088 --> 01:00:59.168
<i>I am Picasso,
the famous Picasso.</i>

508
01:00:59.288 --> 01:01:01.288
This is my car.
l am the driver.

509
01:01:01.448 --> 01:01:04.729
These are my dreams.
l bought them from God.

510
01:01:05.409 --> 01:01:07.089
You like my hat?

511
01:01:08.649 --> 01:01:12.609
<i>I am Modigliani,
the crazy Italian fuck.</i>

512
01:01:16.689 --> 01:01:19.890
<i>Sit down, Matador.
You're scaring the peasants.</i>

513
01:01:37.251 --> 01:01:41.331
Her neck is not so long.
She has her father's neck. Short.

514
01:01:42.611 --> 01:01:45.451
-Yes...
-l like...

515
01:01:45.571 --> 01:01:47.131
Excuse me.

516
01:01:47.251 --> 01:01:49.612
<i>-Not so long.
-Okay, l know.</i>

517
01:01:50.372 --> 01:01:53.892
Go back. Out of my way.
Thank you.

518
01:02:03.253 --> 01:02:05.853
-Don't touch my painting.
-You're ruining it because...

519
01:02:05.973 --> 01:02:08.253
I'm the painter.
You're ruining the painting.

520
01:02:08.413 --> 01:02:11.653
lt's very wide.
Of course you're the painter.

521
01:02:17.213 --> 01:02:19.574
You paint it.

522
01:02:23.894 --> 01:02:26.854
You like it?
it's for you.

523
01:02:31.374 --> 01:02:34.735
I'm not paying for this.

524
01:03:07.857 --> 01:03:09.057
To Livorno.

525
01:03:49.500 --> 01:03:53.780
You promised you
wouldn't let me die here.

526
01:05:39.787 --> 01:05:43.227
<i>Maurice, you're safe.</i>

527
01:05:46.787 --> 01:05:50.228
<i>Get away from him!
All of you, get out!</i>

528
01:05:50.428 --> 01:05:51.668
Get out!

529
01:05:52.388 --> 01:05:54.268
Get out!

530
01:05:54.428 --> 01:05:58.348
Want him to become what you've
become? You think it's romantic?

531
01:05:59.228 --> 01:06:02.228
lt's how it should be?
Get out!

532
01:06:08.109 --> 01:06:09.389
Have some water.

533
01:06:24.990 --> 01:06:26.630
How do you feel?

534
01:06:27.190 --> 01:06:29.030
I don't know.

535
01:06:31.590 --> 01:06:33.910
They said l shouldn't leave you.

536
01:06:34.630 --> 01:06:38.791
So l won't.

537
01:06:39.551 --> 01:06:41.791
Never again.

538
01:06:48.391 --> 01:06:54.872
-The rain speaks.
-Really? What does it say?

539
01:07:02.192 --> 01:07:03.992
<i>It says, "Don't cry",
my love.</i>

540
01:07:06.793 --> 01:07:08.633
Modi is here.

541
01:07:32.034 --> 01:07:36.155
-How do you feel?
-Alive.

542
01:07:38.515 --> 01:07:40.275
You should thank Zbo.

543
01:07:41.355 --> 01:07:43.155
He gave us the money
to come here.

544
01:07:45.235 --> 01:07:48.155
If he'd only sold my work
he could come here more often.

545
01:07:49.795 --> 01:07:52.196
<i>Well, i'm trying.</i>

546
01:07:53.156 --> 01:07:56.596
That was the most beautiful meal.
Thank you. Great stuff.

547
01:07:57.876 --> 01:08:00.276
<i>So, tell us, what else
is happening is Paris?</i>

548
01:08:00.796 --> 01:08:04.116
Nothing new.
The same as before.

549
01:08:04.276 --> 01:08:07.517
Just watching everyone get ready
for the competition.

550
01:08:10.757 --> 01:08:14.037
<i>-Well, Modi...
-No.</i>

551
01:08:18.277 --> 01:08:20.597
I'm going to rest.
I'm tired.

552
01:08:22.918 --> 01:08:26.398
-Remember; no drink.
-No drink.

553
01:08:34.558 --> 01:08:36.279
-l love you.
-l love you.

554
01:08:38.199 --> 01:08:40.399
Good night.
See you later.

555
01:08:43.599 --> 01:08:49.079
-May l see your work?
-What for? You never sell anything.

556
01:08:50.239 --> 01:08:52.000
Beautiful.

557
01:08:52.680 --> 01:08:54.840
A poetry.

558
01:08:55.000 --> 01:08:59.560
<i>Modi, prepare yourself. We're gonna
need all of this in Paris...</i>

559
01:08:59.840 --> 01:09:03.120
for your one-man show.

560
01:09:05.080 --> 01:09:07.361
You heard me right.

561
01:09:07.881 --> 01:09:11.121
Bertha Veil loved the nudes
so much...

562
01:09:11.241 --> 01:09:14.641
She wants to hang
everything you have.

563
01:09:20.201 --> 01:09:22.042
Did you hear me?

564
01:09:22.162 --> 01:09:28.802
Bertha Veil is giving you your
very own one-man show.

565
01:10:10.925 --> 01:10:12.925
<i>Bravo, Modigliani!</i>

566
01:10:13.645 --> 01:10:15.605
They're exquisite.

567
01:10:15.725 --> 01:10:20.565
<i>Jeanne, great Jeanne.</i>

568
01:10:20.765 --> 01:10:23.566
<i>Mrs. Veil,
you're the organizer?</i>

569
01:10:23.726 --> 01:10:26.446
You know l am.
You live just across the street.

570
01:10:26.606 --> 01:10:29.486
You shall remove a painting
from your gallery window.

571
01:10:29.646 --> 01:10:32.006
I will do not.

572
01:10:37.447 --> 01:10:39.687
Come back with this tomorrow.

573
01:10:39.807 --> 01:10:41.567
If you don't remove
the paintings...

574
01:10:41.647 --> 01:10:43.527
My men will do it for you.

575
01:10:43.567 --> 01:10:45.207
And we'll close down the show.

576
01:10:45.327 --> 01:10:47.047
This is outrageous.

577
01:10:47.127 --> 01:10:50.847
<i>Are they pictures of your mother,
your sister?</i>

578
01:10:53.768 --> 01:10:55.568
Do as he says.

579
01:10:56.488 --> 01:10:58.008
Do as he says.

580
01:11:04.208 --> 01:11:05.608
<i>Why, Modi?</i>

581
01:11:12.129 --> 01:11:13.729
I'm impressed.

582
01:11:17.089 --> 01:11:20.529
<i>By the way, l hope
you won't be offended...</i>

583
01:11:20.729 --> 01:11:23.050
the painting you gave me
as a gift...

584
01:11:23.210 --> 01:11:25.570
The one Jeanne brought me...

585
01:11:25.690 --> 01:11:29.290
The other night l was
inspired by something...

586
01:11:29.450 --> 01:11:33.410
<i>a felt hat.
Yes, a felt hat.</i>

587
01:11:34.290 --> 01:11:38.771
l didn't have a canvas.
it was 4 in the morning.

588
01:11:38.931 --> 01:11:40.971
<i>Make your point, Spanish.</i>

589
01:11:42.491 --> 01:11:44.971
l used your painting.

590
01:11:53.572 --> 01:11:55.252
Do you forgive me?

591
01:12:10.453 --> 01:12:12.653
Let's go.

592
01:12:20.413 --> 01:12:22.654
I think l like
the new Modigliani.

593
01:12:22.934 --> 01:12:25.134
<i>Yes, l think l do.</i>

594
01:12:26.534 --> 01:12:28.294
Let's look around.

595
01:12:40.655 --> 01:12:42.415
I'm tired.

596
01:12:43.055 --> 01:12:46.215
I'm not.

597
01:12:46.855 --> 01:12:49.255
That's because
you're not pregnant.

598
01:12:55.696 --> 01:12:57.976
<i>-So.
-Go, go.</i>

599
01:12:58.616 --> 01:13:00.816
<i>-See you later. Bye!
-Can you stop the bus, please.</i>

600
01:13:04.296 --> 01:13:08.697
<i>Tell me, Modigliani.
How does a blind man paint?</i>

601
01:13:11.737 --> 01:13:13.377
You don't know.

602
01:13:20.737 --> 01:13:24.738
He paints what nobody sees!
What nobody sees!

603
01:13:32.298 --> 01:13:33.258
Go!

604
01:13:50.939 --> 01:13:52.019
What?

605
01:13:52.659 --> 01:13:54.660
He gave your baby
to the welfare.

606
01:13:54.980 --> 01:13:56.020
What?

607
01:13:56.100 --> 01:13:59.180
Your baby. Your beautiful little
girl is now in strange hands.

608
01:14:00.060 --> 01:14:02.700
And all because you can't
live a normal life...

609
01:14:02.780 --> 01:14:04.980
Like the rest of the world
around you.

610
01:14:11.221 --> 01:14:14.621
Get out and show your face!
Show your face!

611
01:14:17.741 --> 01:14:20.501
You see me?
You see the Jew?

612
01:14:20.661 --> 01:14:22.781
Go away or i'll call the police.

613
01:14:22.901 --> 01:14:24.582
You'd better call the police.

614
01:14:41.783 --> 01:14:45.063
-Where is my baby?
-You get away from me.

615
01:14:48.063 --> 01:14:49.783
Where is my baby?

616
01:14:49.943 --> 01:14:51.703
Somewhere where
you'll never find her.

617
01:14:57.664 --> 01:15:02.944
Go on.

618
01:15:03.104 --> 01:15:05.104
Do it.
Do it.

619
01:15:05.544 --> 01:15:07.704
No one's here.

620
01:15:08.424 --> 01:15:13.865
Tomorrow you can tell the whole
world a Jew threatened your life.

621
01:15:14.785 --> 01:15:16.985
A Jew.
Do it!

622
01:15:20.305 --> 01:15:21.705
Do it!

623
01:15:21.905 --> 01:15:23.945
Do it!

624
01:15:26.146 --> 01:15:28.946
I'm gonna ask you one more time.
Where is my baby?

625
01:15:29.106 --> 01:15:31.106
You...

626
01:15:31.266 --> 01:15:35.586
You have neither resource
nor conditions to raise her.

627
01:15:53.187 --> 01:15:54.628
Watch me.

628
01:17:26.514 --> 01:17:28.354
I forgive you.

629
01:26:38.990 --> 01:26:42.150
Modi?
Hello? Have you finished yet?

630
01:26:42.310 --> 01:26:46.551
Yes and l want you to take
the painting to the competition.

631
01:26:46.871 --> 01:26:50.791
What about you?
Remember it starts today.

632
01:26:50.991 --> 01:26:53.511
Don't let the painting
out of your sight.

633
01:26:54.031 --> 01:26:56.831
<i>-Where are you?
-City Hall.</i>

634
01:26:56.911 --> 01:26:57.991
What for?

635
01:26:58.111 --> 01:27:00.032
Marriage license.
I'm going to marry Jeanne.

636
01:27:01.432 --> 01:27:03.952
<i>Silence, uh?</i>

637
01:27:38.034 --> 01:27:39.914
<i>Modigliani,
marriage license.</i>

638
01:27:40.114 --> 01:27:41.394
<i>Yes, sit down.</i>

639
01:27:57.235 --> 01:27:58.955
-You're getting married?
-Yes.

640
01:27:59.595 --> 01:28:01.436
Me too.

641
01:28:02.036 --> 01:28:03.556
Congratulations.

642
01:28:13.996 --> 01:28:16.037
Excuse me.

643
01:28:19.797 --> 01:28:21.197
You have children?

644
01:28:22.197 --> 01:28:24.397
I have one and one on the way.

645
01:28:26.637 --> 01:28:28.277
Lt's important children.

646
01:28:28.717 --> 01:28:31.038
Very important.

647
01:28:40.758 --> 01:28:42.358
Go away!

648
01:28:42.678 --> 01:28:45.799
<i>I'm crazy, you know?
I will do something.</i>

649
01:28:46.039 --> 01:28:47.359
Go away!

650
01:29:01.280 --> 01:29:02.920
<i>Excuse me,
i'm going to the corner.</i>

651
01:29:22.041 --> 01:29:24.841
<i>No, no. You do not touch
this painting.</i>

652
01:29:25.041 --> 01:29:26.521
it's my painting.

653
01:29:26.681 --> 01:29:28.681
What's going on here?

654
01:29:30.001 --> 01:29:32.802
Lt's the police.
They get the painting.

655
01:29:32.962 --> 01:29:34.402
If something happens
to this painting...

656
01:29:34.522 --> 01:29:36.882
You'll spend the rest of my life
as a eunuch.

657
01:29:37.002 --> 01:29:39.122
A eunuch!
Understood?

658
01:29:41.922 --> 01:29:43.722
<i>Good.
Bye-bye, eunuch.</i>

659
01:29:47.483 --> 01:29:48.763
Eunuch.

660
01:29:56.323 --> 01:29:57.843
Be careful.

661
01:29:59.003 --> 01:30:00.843
What about the others?

662
01:30:01.083 --> 01:30:03.884
-They're hanged.
-All of them?

663
01:30:05.004 --> 01:30:07.604
All of them.

664
01:30:09.644 --> 01:30:13.324
<i>So, now we'll know.</i>

665
01:30:17.445 --> 01:30:18.925
Monsieur?

666
01:30:27.805 --> 01:30:30.165
-What time is it?
-Closing time.

667
01:30:30.285 --> 01:30:31.606
You must leave now.

668
01:30:32.326 --> 01:30:36.606
<i>Madame, l must have my
marriage license today.</i>

669
01:30:36.726 --> 01:30:39.966
<i>-Monday, nine o'clock.
-Don't understand. l need it today.</i>

670
01:30:40.126 --> 01:30:42.486
l need it today.

671
01:30:42.646 --> 01:30:45.766
<i>Monsieur, we all have families.
We need to go home too.</i>

672
01:30:45.886 --> 01:30:49.487
l have a baby coming
any day.

673
01:30:50.727 --> 01:30:54.167
And l have a beautiful daughter.
Please.

674
01:30:57.087 --> 01:30:59.047
Please.

675
01:31:00.767 --> 01:31:03.368
<i>You are a painter, aren't you?</i>

676
01:31:05.288 --> 01:31:07.528
Yes.

677
01:31:08.248 --> 01:31:11.648
-Me too.
-l can see that.

678
01:31:13.608 --> 01:31:15.168
Very well...

679
01:31:18.129 --> 01:31:21.849
<i>-sign here.
-Thank you, ma'am.</i>

680
01:31:41.370 --> 01:31:43.250
What's wrong with it?

681
01:31:43.410 --> 01:31:46.450
The color.
Flash with my painting.

682
01:33:03.496 --> 01:33:04.416
Cheers.

683
01:33:16.376 --> 01:33:18.377
You will pay for the drink.

684
01:33:18.537 --> 01:33:22.017
I have five thousand Francs.
Today l buy everybody a drink.

685
01:33:40.658 --> 01:33:41.898
To Livorno.

686
01:34:13.740 --> 01:34:15.260
Cheers.

687
01:34:33.021 --> 01:34:35.182
<i>Jeanne, here!</i>

688
01:34:40.302 --> 01:34:42.542
-ls he here?
-l thought he'd be with you.

689
01:34:42.702 --> 01:34:43.942
<i>No, no...</i>

690
01:34:51.343 --> 01:34:54.583
<i>Mommy, thank you so much.</i>

691
01:34:55.303 --> 01:34:58.303
l thought maybe she
would bring him luck.

692
01:34:58.703 --> 01:35:00.103
Thank you.

693
01:35:01.863 --> 01:35:04.464
Where is the great Modigliani?

694
01:35:12.944 --> 01:35:15.904
The trumpets of silence.

695
01:35:16.144 --> 01:35:18.504
Ships of peace
make me sleep.

696
01:35:18.664 --> 01:35:20.745
The cradle swings
when the morning comes.

697
01:35:21.585 --> 01:35:23.945
I wrote that myself when
l was alone in the night.

698
01:35:24.145 --> 01:35:27.305
But no longer.

699
01:35:28.665 --> 01:35:31.225
Today is the prove
that i'm a rich man.

700
01:35:31.345 --> 01:35:33.145
Rich beyond belief.

701
01:36:03.947 --> 01:36:07.468
<i>Ladies and gentlemen, attention.
it's time.</i>

702
01:36:11.588 --> 01:36:15.668
<i>Ladies and gentlemen,
l give you Soutine.</i>

703
01:36:26.829 --> 01:36:28.989
Diego Rivera.

704
01:36:29.909 --> 01:36:31.909
"Mexico".

705
01:36:51.031 --> 01:36:53.711
Kisling.
"Fear".

706
01:37:05.592 --> 01:37:08.552
Utrillo.
"Madness".

707
01:37:25.833 --> 01:37:28.073
Picasso.
Title...

708
01:37:29.753 --> 01:37:31.793
"Modigliani".

709
01:38:13.276 --> 01:38:17.116
<i>And finally,
l give you Modigliani.</i>

710
01:38:17.916 --> 01:38:22.637
Title; "Jeanne".

711
01:38:32.237 --> 01:38:36.158
<i>When l know your soul,
i'll paint your eyes.</i>

712
01:41:39.370 --> 01:41:40.970
Don't worry.

713
01:41:41.570 --> 01:41:43.170
My hands...

714
01:41:44.610 --> 01:41:46.410
My hands.

715
01:41:49.130 --> 01:41:50.490
You'll be okay.

716
01:41:58.171 --> 01:42:00.211
Jeanne...

717
01:42:01.131 --> 01:42:05.651
<i>lt's okay.
Sleep, dear. Sleep.</i>

718
01:42:10.172 --> 01:42:14.812
In my pocket.

719
01:42:26.133 --> 01:42:28.853
I wanted to surprise you.

720
01:42:32.173 --> 01:42:36.813
I'll always be your wife.

721
01:42:36.933 --> 01:42:38.814
Modi!

722
01:42:39.054 --> 01:42:41.494
lt's us!

723
01:42:41.614 --> 01:42:43.294
I can't see nothing.

724
01:42:48.414 --> 01:42:51.454
-In the name of God!
-What happened?

725
01:42:51.534 --> 01:42:53.735
Get away from him.

726
01:42:53.895 --> 01:42:55.535
He needs a doctor.

727
01:43:06.735 --> 01:43:09.296
Don't take him from me.

728
01:43:12.176 --> 01:43:15.216
Don't take him!

729
01:43:18.216 --> 01:43:20.896
Don't take him from me!

730
01:43:21.496 --> 01:43:24.417
Don't take him from me!

731
01:43:26.097 --> 01:43:32.417
Don't take him from me!
Please.

732
01:43:43.298 --> 01:43:44.658
Watch his head.

733
01:43:45.658 --> 01:43:48.298
<i>Modi, stay with us.</i>

734
01:43:50.418 --> 01:43:51.818
<i>Oh, my God.</i>

735
01:44:32.981 --> 01:44:34.261
Excuse us.

736
01:45:05.183 --> 01:45:10.224
Jeanne...

737
01:45:13.184 --> 01:45:16.944
Always and forever.

738
01:45:20.264 --> 01:45:22.264
I'm here.

739
01:45:23.464 --> 01:45:25.945
I'm here.

740
01:46:09.468 --> 01:46:11.628
lt's time to end this madness.

741
01:46:52.070 --> 01:46:57.031
<i>Wait for me, my love.
Wait for me.</i>

742
01:47:41.794 --> 01:47:43.434
Wait...

743
01:48:46.318 --> 01:48:47.558
Jeanne...

744
01:48:50.398 --> 01:48:53.558
I offer my
deepest sympathies.

745
01:48:54.158 --> 01:48:57.399
I can't imagine
how you feel.

746
01:48:59.559 --> 01:49:01.719
You know what l feel?

747
01:49:03.839 --> 01:49:07.239
<i>Pablo, shall l tell you?</i>

748
01:49:11.520 --> 01:49:14.880
l feel nothing.

749
01:49:17.840 --> 01:49:20.680
I have a baby in my belly...

750
01:49:23.320 --> 01:49:25.761
Another heart beating...

751
01:49:27.401 --> 01:49:30.321
Another soul craving...

752
01:49:32.561 --> 01:49:36.761
<i>and i'm empty,
like your glass.</i>

753
01:49:42.242 --> 01:49:44.762
You'll go home.

754
01:49:46.962 --> 01:49:52.162
You'll always live a full
and rich life.

755
01:49:54.322 --> 01:49:59.043
But l swear to God...
when your time comes...

756
01:50:01.363 --> 01:50:04.643
When you leave
at your death bed...

757
01:50:08.163 --> 01:50:11.604
The name Modigliani...

758
01:50:12.284 --> 01:50:14.684
Will not be far
from your lips.

759
01:50:23.284 --> 01:50:26.565
You can never paint
over this night.

760
01:50:26.685 --> 01:50:28.365
lt belongs to him.

761
01:50:50.246 --> 01:50:56.887
<i>l saw him dance once
by the statue of Balzac.</i>

762
01:50:58.407 --> 01:51:04.527
<i>So beautiful his face,
so graceful his arms...</i>

763
01:51:05.807 --> 01:51:10.327
<i>as he swayed to the song,
he smiled...</i>

764
01:51:11.488 --> 01:51:16.728
<i>He was all the things
l was once.</i>

765
01:51:18.248 --> 01:51:24.088
<i>So, l stole that moment,
and locked it away in my mind...</i>

766
01:51:24.528 --> 01:51:30.569
<i>to be there, to comfort me
in my empty days.</i>

767
01:51:32.009 --> 01:51:35.209
<i>Auguste Renoir.</i>

768
01:51:51.850 --> 01:51:56.130
Papa sends you all the love
of the world.

769
01:51:58.491 --> 01:52:05.371
<i>When you grow up, you'll feel
our love wherever you go.</i>

770
01:52:34.933 --> 01:52:37.173
<i>l want you to know...</i>

771
01:52:38.853 --> 01:52:40.613
<i>and try to understand...</i>

772
01:52:42.454 --> 01:52:44.454
<i>try to forgive me.</i>
